  "title": "DigitalOcean Kubernetes application cluster",
  "description": "A documentation-oriented DOKS reference architecture showing public ingress, a managed control plane, three editable worker-node frames, application pods, managed PostgreSQL, and Spaces object storage.",
  "template_brief": "DIGITALOCEAN KUBERNETES REFERENCE\n\nARCHITECTURE INTENT\nInternet -> DigitalOcean Load Balancer -> Gateway / Ingress -> application pods.\nThe DOKS control plane is fully managed by DigitalOcean.\nIllustrative pod placement uses three worker-node frames; the Kubernetes scheduler may reschedule replicas across workers.\nManaged PostgreSQL and Spaces remain outside the Kubernetes workload boundary.\n\nDOCUMENTATION\nhttps://docs.digitalocean.com/products/kubernetes/details/managed/\nhttps://docs.digitalocean.com/products/kubernetes/how-to/add-load-balancers/\nhttps://docs.digitalocean.com/products/kubernetes/how-to/use-spaces/\nhttps://docs.digitalocean.com/products/kubernetes/how-to/data-storage/\nhttps://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/\nhttps://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/ingress/",
